% This is a placeholder for the ultrasonic response Simulink subsystem.
% In a real MATLAB/Simulink environment, this would be a graphical subsystem
% implementing the ultrasonic time-of-flight, amplitude, and phase shift model.

% The subsystem should model:
% - Time-of-Flight (ToF): affected by speed of sound changes in battery materials
% - Signal Amplitude: affected by attenuation from degradation mechanisms
% - Phase Shift: affected by material property changes
%
% Inputs:
% - Excitation pulse timing
% - Degradation mode parameters (speed of sound factor, attenuation factor, phase factor)
% - Ultrasonic frequency and bandwidth parameters
%
% Outputs:
% - Time-of-Flight measurement
% - Signal amplitude
% - Phase shift

% The ultrasonic response can be modeled as:
% tof = 2 * path_length / speed_of_sound
% where speed_of_sound = nominal_sos * sos_factor (from degradation mode)
%
% amplitude = transmitted_amplitude / attenuation_factor
% where attenuation_factor comes from degradation mode
%
% phase_shift = base_phase_shift + phase_factor
% where phase_factor comes from degradation mode

% This file represents the intended structure. Actual implementation requires
% using MATLAB Simulink editor to create the graphical subsystem with:
% - Gain blocks for degradation mode factors
% - Delay blocks for time-of-flight simulation
% - Math operations for attenuation and phase calculations
% - Parameter references to workspace or data dictionary